WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.650
After the 1960s, UK manufacturing
employment declined drastically.

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.590
Inner cities lost jobs and people.

3
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.570
In 1980, a new Act provided for
urban development corporations,

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.810
to secure the regeneration of their areas.

5
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.110
In London's Docklands, an
appointed board led the work,

6
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.070
not the elected council.

7
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.550
New offices and homes arrived.

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.870
Then came neighbourhood partnerships,
the London 2012 Olympic Park,

9
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.260
and levelling up.

10
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.730
Forty years on, has any
of it closed the gap?

11
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.050
Or did only London benefit?

12
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.010
In this mission, you'll compare four eras:

13
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.650
who led, which tools they
used, and who gained.

14
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.470
Then you'll judge each
against the evidence.

15
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.400
Your mission: evaluate whether forty
years of urban policy closed the gap.
